8. Revised Technical Approach
Extraction Module:
Real-Time Price Monitoring:
Query gTrade’s price feed every 5 minutes using Web3.py for current trade execution and monitoring.
Historical Data & Technical Analysis:
Fetch historical price data using yfinance and calculate technical indicators (e.g., RSI, MACD, EMA, Bollinger Bands) using pandas‑ta.
Spec Sheet Revisions:
Technical Stack Update:
TA‑Lib has been removed in favor of yfinance and pandas‑ta for historical data analysis, while gTrade remains the source for real-time price data.
Multi-User Preparedness:
Database Schema: Updated the schema to include a user_id column in both the trades and sessions tables, with corresponding foreign key constraints linking to a placeholder users table. This prepares the system for future multi-user support.
Codebase & Logging:
Modules and logging have been updated to accept and log a user_id parameter, ensuring that the backend is structured for a scalable, multi-user platform.
These changes lay the groundwork for transitioning from a single-user bot to a full platform (ggbots.ai) for building and managing AI Trading Agents without incurring significant technical debt.



9. Implementation of Browser-Use & Local LLM for Automated TradingView Extraction
Research & Strategic Decisions
Conducted research on Browser-Use (Playwright-based) and confirmed its feasibility for TradingView data extraction.
Evaluated two approaches:
Full GPT-4o API for both login and extraction.
Hybrid Approach (Chosen):
Headful login using TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat for secure, local credential handling.
Headless extraction using GPT-4o API for TradingView chart parsing.
Automated session re-login on expiry.
The hybrid approach was selected for security (local credential handling), cost reduction, and scalability (multi-user future-proofing).

